<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xi'an</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xi'an is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a> plain. Nearby lay the Western Zhou capitals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fengjing">Fengjing</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haojing">Haojing</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianyang">Xianyang</a> and the great Han and Tang capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, on whose site much of the modern city stands. Its present walls date from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>, and the Terracotta Army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-shi-huang">First Emperor of Qin</a> lies to its east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xian.jpg" alt="Xi'an" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:City_wall_of_Xi%27an_51550-Xian_(27959363326).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
